### 2026-09-11 — Generated music per episode (PR #3)

- Built: `scripts/compose-music.py` (numpy + lame) — a piano composer giving every episode its own key,
  tempo, meter, texture and reverb room. Iterated from "one pattern, too busy" to background music under
  a voice: sparse, soft attack, pad-led, normalized to about −21 dBFS. Episode 00 later moved from D
  minor to a warm G major on request.
- Files: added `scripts/compose-music.py`; regenerated all four `docs/3d/episodes/*.mp3`.
- Tests: spectral check of every track (loudness, brightness, onset rate, detected pulse, key) plus
  `npm run test:e2e`.
- Merged: https://github.com/eleken-git/design-process-help/pull/3
- Notes / follow-ups: regenerate one track with `python3 scripts/compose-music.py <episode-id>`.

### 2026-09-11 — Music in the 3D player stopped dropping out (PR #4)

- Built: root cause was the animation loop reseeking the audio every frame while
  `python3 -m http.server` served no Range requests, so the track restarted 60 times a second (589 seeks
  in 10 s, `currentTime` stuck at 0). The track is now seeked only on an explicit user action, and while
  it plays the animation follows the audio clock. The muted button no longer flips `musicOn` when it
  means "enable sound". Replaced the local docs server with `scripts/serve-docs.mjs` (Range support).
- Files: `docs/3d/engine.js`, added `scripts/serve-docs.mjs`, `package.json` (`npm run docs`),
  `.claude/launch.json`, `playwright.config.ts`, `tests/player.spec.ts`.
- Tests: two new player specs, red before the fix and green after; 0 seeks in 10 s at 60 and at 51 fps.
- Merged: https://github.com/eleken-git/design-process-help/pull/4

